# Saas-Booking Project Rules (Do Not Break UI/Logic)

## Non-negotiables
- Do NOT refactor or rewrite components unless explicitly asked.
- Keep existing API contracts intact (routes, DTO shapes, status codes). If a change is needed, propose it first.
- Avoid "big rewrites": prefer minimal diffs and targeted changes.
- Never remove functionality to "simplify".

## UI / CSS safety
- Do NOT rename existing CSS classes without updating all usages.
- Do NOT switch styling system (no Tailwind migration, no UI library swap) unless explicitly requested.
- If changing layout, keep DOM structure stable as much as possible.
- Always preserve RTL behavior.

## Data / Backend safety
- Do NOT change Mongo schemas, indexes, or auth logic without a clear migration plan.
- Do NOT touch auth cookies/JWT strategy unless explicitly requested.

## Workflow
- When implementing a feature: 
  1) Identify the exact files to touch.
  2) Make smallest change possible.
  3) Provide a short "how to test" checklist (Postman + UI).
